<h2>Installation Notes</h2>

<p>
    There is little "installation" actually required except for enabling Sushi.</p>
<p>
    Installing Sushi requires both node and npm to be functioning.  Under local windows node and npm can be installed if absent and under Azure/Windows they are already available though it may be necessary to set an environment variable to specify the version of node to use.
    Under Azure/Unix it is difficult to make node available to a WebApp.  Whatever system the app try to find sushi and provide a suitable message if it cannot.
    Generally you can install sushi manually using the usual <br /> <i>npm install -g fsh-sushi</i><br />  you can specify a location for the install by adding <i>"--prefix D:\home"</i>.
</p>

<p> Once sushi is installed the path can be specified on the Settup page though if left blank the app will search for sushi before giving up.

</p>

